R['results']=res
R['interpretation']=R['interpretation']+" Q1 (HCN/HCO+ at matched J): the ratio at matched beam is lower at the AGN-hosting S nucleus than at N at every J (3-2 at 0.25\": N 1.03, S 0.48; at 6.5\": 0.54 vs 0.39; 4-3 at 6.5\": 0.43 vs 0.32; deblended S/N ~0.6-0.75 at 2-1, 3-2 and 4-3), and falls ~25% per J step everywhere (midpoint 0.58, 0.45, 0.33 at 10\"), so there is no HCN/HCO+ enhancement at the S nucleus, agreeing with Harada+2018. The only enhancement is tentative: the blue-wing blob 1.9\" S of S has HCN/HCO+ = 1.4+-0.3 vs 0.38 in the S core (~3 sigma), qualitatively as expected for shock heating of outflowing gas (Nishimura+2024) but at the level that team-a's 1.8 is biased high by peak selection. The N-nucleus ratio >1 at 0.25\" is a compact HCN-bright core. Ladder ratios alone allow A=N(HCN)/N(HCO+) from <1 (n>=3e6) to ~4 (n~1e4-1e5): abundance versus excitation is undecided without H13CN."
R['caveats']=R['caveats']+["Q1: ratios at 10\" and 6.5\" merge N, S and Bridge (5.2\" apart); only the 0.25-0.94\" 3-2 ratios and the template-deblended 2-1/4-3 values refer to individual regions. The deblending assumes the Xb4d 3-2 zone morphology holds at J=2,4 (chi2_red 35-240).","Q1: Xb4f/Xb47/Xb55 are not corrected for missing short-spacing flux (negative bowls: annulus 8-20\" sums are negative at 6.5-10\"); HCN/HCO+ is insensitive to this at N/S/Bridge (p0003) but the clump ratios and any 'disk' ratio (r>8\") are not reliable. Band 7 primary-beam correction is large at r>8\" (PB~0.5)."]
json.dump(R,open(P,'w'),indent=1); print(len(res))
